      "content": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Strict//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-strict.dtd\">\n<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\">\n<head profile=\"http://gmpg.org/xfn/11\">\n    <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=utf-8\"/>\n    <title>Byzantine Eventual Consistency and the Fundamental Limits of Peer-to-Peer Databases &mdash; Martin Kleppmann&rsquo;s publications</title>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"screen, print, handheld\" href=\"/css/typography.css\" />\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"screen\" href=\"/css/style.css\" />\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"all\" href=\"/css/pygments-default.css\" />\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"all\" href=\"/css/ansi2html.css\" />\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"all\" href=\"/css/customizations.css?5\" />\n<!--[if lt IE 8]>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/css/ie.css\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"screen\" charset=\"utf-8\" />\n<![endif]-->\n<link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/rss+xml\" title=\"RSS\" href=\"https://feeds.feedburner.com/martinkl?format=xml\" title=\"Martin Kleppmann's blog\" />\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" async\n    src=\"https://cdn.mathjax.org/mathjax/latest/MathJax.js?config=TeX-AMS_CHTML\">\n</script>\n\n\n    <!-- Info on meta tags for Google Scholar: https://www.monperrus.net/martin/accurate+bibliographic+metadata+and+google+scholar -->\n    <meta name=\"citation_title\" content=\"Byzantine Eventual Consistency and the Fundamental Limits of Peer-to-Peer Databases\" /> \n    <meta name=\"citation_publication_date\" content=\"2020-12-01\" /> \n    <meta name=\"citation_authors\" content=\"Martin Kleppmann and Heidi Howard\" /> \n    <meta name=\"citation_pdf_url\" content=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.00472\" /> \n    \n</head>\n\n<body class=\"wordpress\">\n    <div id=\"page\">\n        <p id=\"top\">\n    <a id=\"to-content\" href=\"#content\" title=\"Skip to content\">Skip to content</a>\n</p>\n\n<div id=\"header\">\n    <div class=\"wrapper\">\n        <strong id=\"blog-title\">\n            <a href=\"/\" title=\"Home\" rel=\"home\">Martin Kleppmann</a>\n        </strong>\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n<div id=\"sub-header\">\n    <div class=\"wrapper\">\n        <div id=\"navigation\">\n            <ul>\n                <li class=\"page_item\"><a href=\"/student-projects.html\" title=\"Student Projects\">Student Projects</a></li>\n                <li class=\"page_item\"><a href=\"/contact.html\" title=\"About/Contact\">About/Contact</a></li>\n                <li class=\"page_item\"><a href=\"/supporters.html\" title=\"Supporters\">Supporters</a></li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n<hr class=\"divider\">\n\n\n        <div class=\"wrapper\">\n            <div id=\"content\">\n                <h1>Byzantine Eventual Consistency and the Fundamental Limits of Peer-to-Peer Databases</h1>\n\n                <p>Martin Kleppmann and Heidi Howard</p>\n\n                <p>\n                  \n                    arXiv:2012.00472 [cs.DC],\n                  \n                  \n                  December 2020.\n                </p>\n\n                \n\n                <ul>\n                  \n                    <li><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.00472\">Paper (open access)</a></li>\n                  \n                  \n                  \n                  \n                  \n                  \n                  \n                  \n                </ul>\n\n                <ul>\n  <li><a href=\"https://martin.kleppmann.com/2020/12/02/bloom-filter-hash-graph-sync.html\">Blog post</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n\n<p>Sybil attacks, in which a large number of adversary-controlled nodes join a network, are a concern\nfor many peer-to-peer database systems, necessitating expensive countermeasures such as\nproof-of-work. However, there is a category of database applications that are, by design, immune to\nSybil attacks because they can tolerate arbitrary numbers of Byzantine-faulty nodes. In this paper,\nwe characterize this category of applications using a consistency model we call Byzantine Eventual\nConsistency (BEC). We introduce an algorithm that guarantees BEC based on Byzantine causal\nbroadcast, prove its correctness, and demonstrate near-optimal performance in a prototype\nimplementation.</p>\n\n            </div>\n\n            <div id=\"sidebar\">\n                <div id=\"carrington-subscribe\" class=\"widget\">\n    <h2 class=\"widget-title\">Subscribe</h2>\n    <a class=\"feed\" title=\"RSS 2.0 feed for posts\" rel=\"alternate\" href=\"http://feeds.feedburner.com/martinkl\">\n        Site <acronym title=\"Really Simple Syndication\">RSS</acronym> feed\n    </a>\n\n    <div class=\"mailing-list-signup\">\n        <p>\n            To find out when I write something new, sign up to receive an\n            <a href=\"https://martinkl.substack.com/\">email notification</a>,\n            <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/martin.kleppmann.com\">follow me on Bluesky</a> or\n            <a href=\"https://nondeterministic.computer/@martin\">Mastodon</a>, or subscribe to the\n            <a href=\"http://feeds.feedburner.com/martinkl\">RSS feed</a>.\n        </p>\n\n        <p class=\"disclaimer\">\n            I won't give your email address to anyone else, won't send you any spam,\n            and you can unsubscribe at any time.\n        </p>\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n<div id=\"primary-sidebar\">\n    <div id=\"book-promo\" class=\"widget\">\n        <h2 class=\"title\">My book</h2>\n        <p><a href=\"http://dataintensive.net\" target=\"_top\"><img src=\"/images/book-cover-small.png\"\n            style=\"border: 1px solid #ddd;\"\n            alt=\"Designing Data-Intensive Applications\" width=\"180\" height=\"238\"/></a></p>\n        <p>My book,\n        <a href=\"http://dataintensive.net\"><em>Designing Data-Intensive Applications</em></a>, has received\n        <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/23466395-designing-data-intensive-applications\">thousands</a>\n        of five-star reviews.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"widget\">\n        <p>I am an Associate Professor working on <a href=\"https://www.inkandswitch.com/local-first/\">local-first software</a>\n        and security protocols at the <a href=\"http://www.cst.cam.ac.uk/\">University of Cambridge</a>.\n        If you find my work useful, please <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/martinkl\">support me on Patreon</a>.</p>\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n                \n\n\n\n\n\n<div id=\"secondary-sidebar\">\n    <div class=\"widget\">\n        <h2 class=\"title\">Recent posts</h2>\n        <ul>\n            \n              <li>07 Oct 2026: <a href=\"/2026/10/07/centre-for-cryptographic-trust-infrastructure.html\">Announcing the Centre for Cryptographic Trust Infrastructure (CCTI)</a></li>\n            \n              <li>08 Dec 2025: <a href=\"/2025/12/08/ai-formal-verification.html\">Prediction: AI will make formal verification go mainstream</a></li>\n            \n              <li>05 Jul 2024: <a href=\"/2024/07/05/pudding-user-discovery-anonymity-networks.html\">Pudding: user discovery for anonymity networks</a></li>\n            \n              <li>04 Jan 2024: <a href=\"/2024/01/04/year-in-review.html\">2023 year in review</a></li>\n            \n              <li>12 Oct 2022: <a href=\"/2022/10/12/verifying-distributed-systems-isabelle.html\">Verifying distributed systems with Isabelle/HOL</a></li>\n            \n            <li><a href=\"/archive.html\">Full archive</a></li>\n        </ul>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"widget\">\n        <h2 class=\"title\">Conference talks</h2>\n        <ul>\n            \n              <li><a href=\"/2026/12/09/opodis-keynote.html\">09 Dec 2026 at 30th Conference on Principles of Distributed Systems (OPODIS)</a></li>\n            \n              <li><a href=\"/2026/09/24/srds-keynote.html\">24 Sep 2026 at 45th International Symposium on Reliable Distributed Systems (SRDS)</a></li>\n            \n              <li><a href=\"/2026/07/12/local-first-conf.html\">12 Jul 2026 at Local-First Conference</a></li>\n            \n              <li><a href=\"/2026/03/17/qcon-keynote-geopolitical-risk.html\">17 Mar 2026 at QCon London</a></li>\n            \n              <li><a href=\"/2026/02/24/local-first-meetup.html\">24 Feb 2026 at Local First (LoFi) meetup</a></li>\n            \n            <li><a href=\"/talks.html\">Full archive</a></li>\n        </ul>\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <hr class=\"divider\" />\n\n<div id=\"footer\">\n    <div class=\"wrapper\">\n        <p id=\"generator-link\">\n            <a rel=\"license\" href=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/\"\n                style=\"float: left; padding: 0.3em 1em 0 0;\"><img alt=\"Creative Commons License\"\n                src=\"/images/creative-commons.png\" width=\"88\" height=\"31\" /></a>\n            Unless otherwise specified, all content on this site is licensed under a\n            <a rel=\"license\" href=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/\">Creative Commons\n                Attribution 3.0 Unported License</a>.\n            Theme borrowed from\n            <span id=\"theme-link\"><a href=\"http://carringtontheme.com\" title=\"Carrington theme for WordPress\">Carrington</a></span>,\n            ported to <a href=\"https://github.com/mojombo/jekyll\">Jekyll</a> by Martin Kleppmann.\n        </p>\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n    </div>\n<script type=\"module\" src=\"https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js/vce701823e78c4301a35b7e07294d87301792088814092\" integrity=\"sha512-UKNk8GbxkABxKcXYuLkO16EleLGUkcvJWtpSNmExE0Too3ZaFAxTscNWEc1OdAv5/BikHawapSCaiD2XCmp+Bw==\" data-cf-beacon='{\"version\":\"2024.11.0\",\"token\":\"ff4e61c8dd38417ca880df455ea4e388\",\"r\":1,\"spa\":2}' crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
